<body>
    <h1>Active Directory/Kerberos - Enable Login in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>This article shows how to enable local login to the device via t=
he Kerberos protocol in IGEL OS.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>Active Directory/Kerberos must be configured as a prerequisite, see <a h=
ref=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/733=
02667/Active+Directory+Kerberos+Configuration+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-re=
source-id=3D"73302667" data-linked-resource-version=3D"3" data-linked-resou=
rce-type=3D"page">Active Directory/Kerberos Configuration in IGEL OS 12</a>=
 .</p>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<p>Menu path: <strong>Security &gt; Logon &gt; Active Directory/Kerberos</s=
trong></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrappe=
r confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image =
confluence-content-image-border image-left" width=3D"340" loading=3D"lazy" =
src=3D"d5b5992a8c790bff6792066d61b55c34692fbac5a6a7e79e3a4b3bdda2d922be" da=
ta-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/7=
3302730/OS12.2_Logon_Active.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D17163646=
80441&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"625" data-width=3D"=
1116" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"733090=
81" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachm=
ent" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"OS12.2_Logon_Active.png" data-ba=
se-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-conten=
t-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302730" data-li=
nked-resource-container-version=3D"9" data-media-id=3D"3d39034e-a74f-419b-a=
b38-3b3fd139f5dd" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"190"></span>
<p></p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>The login can be used for single sign-on in a number of session types (I=
CA, RDP).</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Login to Active Directory domain</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91&nbsp;You can log in to the device via Active Directory.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90&nbsp;You cannot log in to the device via Active Directory. (De=
fault)</p>
<h2 id=3D"ActiveDirectory/Kerberos-EnableLogininIGELOS12-LoginMethods">Logi=
n Methods</h2>
<p><strong>Explicit</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 You can log in with a user name and password. (Default)</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 You cannot log in with a user name and password. If logging in=
 with a smartcard is set up, you can log in with a smartcard.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Remember last user name</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 The login dialog will be pre-populated with the last user name=
 that logged on.&nbsp;<strong>Explicit</strong>&nbsp;must be enabled for th=
is.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The login dialog will not be pre-populated. (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Smartcard</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 You can log in using a smartcard.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 You cannot log in using a smartcard. (Default)<br></p>
<p><strong>Smartcard removal action</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Specifies what action is performed when the smartcard via which the user=
 is logged in is removed.<br>
Possible actions:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Log out</strong>: The user is logged out from the device. (Defau=
lt)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Lock device</strong>: The screen is locked.</p></li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>If the login method is configured and the <strong>Allow system logoff</s=
trong> option is enabled under <strong>System &gt; Power Options &gt; Shutd=
own</strong>, the user can log off the device through the shutdown menu. Fo=
r information on how to access the shutdown menu, see <a href=3D"https://ig=
el-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302824/Commands+Se=
ssion+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302824" data-linked-resou=
rce-version=3D"8" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Commands Session in IG=
EL OS 12</a> . For information on how to configure the shutdown menu, see <=
a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/=
73302742/Shutdown+Settings+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"733027=
42" data-linked-resource-version=3D"4" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">S=
hutdown Settings in IGEL OS 12</a> .</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Automatically perform login</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 The device performs the login automatically on startup. The cr=
edentials provided in <strong>Username for autologin</strong> and <strong>P=
assword for autologin</strong> are <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" da=
ta-ref=3D"573b1555-9be2-4faa-a34f-00765a6789e4">used for</span> Microsoft A=
ctive Directory (AD).</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The login is not performed automatically; a login dialog is di=
splayed.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Username for autologin</strong></p>
<p>The username that is <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"c=
74bc548-ccc7-4132-99e2-ec48a39d7add">used</span> for automatic login.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Password for autologin</strong></p>
<p>The password that is <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"3=
655fbd1-e4e3-4d10-9a8c-ed184a80888f">used</span> for automatic login.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
